    "result": "I implemented `search_products` in `solution.py`, and all 14 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass. I didn't run a coverage check myself, so the 90% gate is unconfirmed, though the tests exercise every branch.\n\nThe query uses a `LIKE` filter with `%`, `_` and `\\` escaped, so they match as ordinary characters. It also applies the stock, `max_price`, ordering, `id` tie-break, `limit` and `offset` rules. Invalid `order_by`, `limit` or `offset` values raise `ValueError`. The function only reads from the database.\n\nI made `limit` and `offset` reject booleans, since `True` is technically an int in Python. The spec doesn't say either way.\n\nOne test, `test_order_name_binary`, has a leftover assertion ending in `or True` that can never fail. The check after it, that names come back sorted, is the real one.",
